<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Threat events (threat events ticket 01, ADR 0015, ADR 0017). Small Misc storyteller events on the player's home map,
       never in the first season (earliestDay 15) and never twice within half a year (minRefireDays 30). Cassandra, Phoebe and
       Randy roll a home Misc incident about every 4.8 days, about 12.5 a year, and pick among those that can fire by weight;
       on a Core-only colony the usable Misc weight is about 10 to 12, so a base chance of 1 is picked about once a year per
       map. DLC Misc events dilute it toward once every year and a half. The worker also refuses while the same kind is
       active on the map, or with its switch or fish stock management off. -->

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>Spearfishing_Urchins</defName>
    <label>urchin outbreak</label>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>Spearfishing.IncidentWorker_Urchins</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1.0</baseChance>
    <earliestDay>15</earliestDay>
    <minRefireDays>30</minRefireDays>
    <letterLabel>Urchins</letterLabel>
    <letterText>Urchins are spreading through the reef and kelp of the {WATER}, grazing it down to bare rock. A bare patch no longer speeds the fish's regrowth, and it spreads until divers cull the urchins. Colonists on Spearfishing work will cull them on their own.</letterText>
    <letterDef>NegativeEvent</letterDef>
  </IncidentDef>

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>Spearfishing_InvasivePredators</defName>
    <label>invasive predators</label>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>Spearfishing.IncidentWorker_InvasivePredators</workerClass>
    <baseChance>1.0</baseChance>
    <earliestDay>15</earliestDay>
    <minRefireDays>30</minRefireDays>
    <letterLabel>Invasive {PREDATOR}</letterLabel>
    <letterText>Invasive {PREDATOR} have turned up in the {WATER}. They eat young fish, so the {WATER} will regrow more slowly as their numbers grow. Spearfishing there culls them, since some of the divers' catches will be {PREDATOR}.</letterText>
    <letterDef>NegativeEvent</letterDef>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
